<title>SWEDEN: Volvo posts 9 pct rise in 1996 profits.</title>
<headline>Volvo posts 9 pct rise in 1996 profits.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo posts its results for the 12 months ending Decebemr 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit before tax/minorities	 14,203 vs   13,048</p>
<p> Sales				     156,060 vs  171,511</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	     4.30 vs     4.00</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		26.90 vs    20.20</p>
<p> Operating costs			 146,999 vs  156,831</p>
<p> Depreciation				5,351 vs    5,656</p>
<p> Operating profit pre non-recurrings 3,710 vs    9,024</p>
<p> Non-recurring items			   0 vs    1,215</p>
<p> Dividend received			   789 vs	351</p>
<p> Result of sale of shares		8,268 vs    1,180</p>
<p> Net interest income (expense)	 1,503 vs	197</p>
<p> Other financial items	   CHARGE  357 vs	321 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					   1,825 vs    3,741</p>
<p> Minorities				     99 vs	 45</p>
<p> Net profit				 12,477 vs    9,262</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found Volvo was expected to post a pre-tax profit including capital gains of 13.6 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
